OP_IRQ_SET on a timer line forgets the tick the call landed in:
a delay of zero arms the line for the tick already counted.
The tick fires every due timer line,
so an Irq armed on one has its deadline ahead of the count.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line is due

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -498,3 +498,3 @@
         uint32_t us = arg[2];
-        irq->deadline = sched_ticks + us / TIMER_US_PER_TICK + (us % TIMER_US_PER_TICK != 0) + 1;
+        irq->deadline = sched_ticks + us / TIMER_US_PER_TICK + (us % TIMER_US_PER_TICK != 0);
     }
